-- title:
--   Level field of k₀-rational q-expansions, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$ containing an element $\zeta_q$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Write $F=$ `fieldBar q M'` for the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, inside the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(\!(X)\!)$, of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ and subgroup `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; $F$ is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is that there is an intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ with the following four properties. First, for $f\in F$ one has $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient $\mathrm{coeff}_n(f)$, $n\in\mathbb{Z}$, lies in the image of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Second, the compositum inside $F$ of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $F$. Third, for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of $F$ (the automorphism satisfying `IsLevelAutBar`, i.e. acting on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ by the $\gamma$-conjugated slash action under the embedding sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, and the identity if no such automorphism exists) maps $F_0$ into $F_0$. Fourth, $F_0$ and $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are linearly disjoint over any finite layer: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K'/k_0$ finite, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to F$ with each $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield of $F$ generated by the image of $K'$, if the $c_i$ are linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$, then all $a_i=0$.
--
--   This is the field of modular functions of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ whose Fourier coefficients lie in the small constant field $k_0$, in the sense of Shimura's fields $F_N$, together with the three properties of it needed later: that it generates $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that it is stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$, and that it is linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over each finite layer. It is the case $q=3$ of the construction of a model over small constants, and is used in the descent and semistable-specialisation arguments for the Jacobian of the modular curve at level $q^2M'$.
